1
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
His family thinks he's crazy. His enemies think he's no
challenge. But she knows he's THE LAST DRAGON.

2
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
The Last Dragon is a action, adventure, music film directed by Michael Schultz.

3
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
A young man searches for the "master" to obtain the final
level of martial arts mastery known as the glow.

4
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Along the way he must fight an evil martial arts expert and rescue a
beautiful singer from an obsessed music promoter.

5
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Leroy Green, played by Taimak.

6
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Laura Charles, played by Vanity.

7
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Eddie Arkadian, played by Christopher Murney.

8
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Sho'nuff / The Shogun of Harlem, played by Julius Carry.

9
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Angela Viracco, played by Faith Prince.

10
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Richie Green, played by Leo O'Brien.

11
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
The Last Dragon (sometimes listed as Berry Gordy's The Last Dragon) is a 1985 American musical martial arts film
directed by Michael Schultz, written by Louis Venosta, and produced by Rupert Hitzig for Berry Gordy.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The film stars Taimak, Vanity, Julius Carry, Christopher
Murney, Keshia Knight Pulliam and Faith Prince.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Choreography was created by Lester Wilson and Lawrence Leritz.

14
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The Last Dragon was released in theaters by Tri-Star Pictures on March 22, 1985.

15
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The film was a financial success despite a mixed reception by critics and is
considered a cult classic, especially in urban Black cinema.

16
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
The film explores themes of martial arts, kung fu,
kidnapping, pop singer, pizzeria.

17
01:42:00,000 --> 01:42:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
